#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-and-tomorrow-sunrise/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "And tomorrow? Sunrise."
msgstr "A jutro? Wschód słońca."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-and-tomorrow-sunrise/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Topic**: \n"
"And tomorrow? Sunrise.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Temat**: \n"
"A jutro? Wschód słońca.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-and-tomorrow-sunrise/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Description**:\n"
"Up until now we told you how a solarpunk city may work, how it would live and how it would face its problems. We spoke about public transports and clean energy, abundance and nature, but now is the time to bring it all together. Bring us all together and get to work.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Angielski opis**:\n"
"Up until now we told you how a solarpunk city may work, how it would live and how it would face its problems. We spoke about public transports and clean energy, abundance and nature, but now is the time to bring it all together. Bring us all together and get to work.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-and-tomorrow-sunrise/index.en.md
msgid ""
"A city where everyone could live a good life, worthy, comfortable and "
"meaningful is a city where the primacy of \"Economy\" over everything else "
"has been dismantled, where people unite to help each other find shared "
"solutions, where \"Technology\" isn't a fetish used to control people and "
"nature, but just a tool among the others, to be used properly. A city where "
"resources aren't grabbed and hoarded by the usual suspects, but shared among "
"everyone equally and ethically. A city where what matters, the only thing "
"that really matters, is caring about others, about nature and urban spaces."
msgstr ""
"A city where everyone could live a good life, worthy, comfortable and "
"meaningful is a city where the primacy of \"Economy\" over everything else "
"has been dismantled, where people unite to help each other find shared "
"solutions, where \"Technology\" isn't a fetish used to control people and "
"nature, but just a tool among the others, to be used properly. A city where "
"resources aren't grabbed and hoarded by the usual suspects, but shared among "
"everyone equally and ethically. A city where what matters, the only thing "
"that really matters, is caring about others, about nature and urban spaces."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-and-tomorrow-sunrise/index.en.md
msgid ""
"A city where small nomadic glasshouses and floating urban gardens can "
"coexist with sun-powered seaplanes, and with clean water and green social "
"spaces."
msgstr ""
"A city where small nomadic glasshouses and floating urban gardens can "
"coexist with sun-powered seaplanes, and with clean water and green social "
"spaces."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-and-tomorrow-sunrise/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Once there wasn't a city like that - and there is no guarantee that one day "
"there will be - but if we join our efforts, if we endure and fight together, "
"one day we will see the dawn over this splendid city."
msgstr ""
"Once there wasn't a city like that - and there is no guarantee that one day "
"there will be - but if we join our efforts, if we endure and fight together, "
"one day we will see the dawn over this splendid city."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-depaving/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Depaving: how to grow fruits and vegetables in the solarpunk city?"
msgstr "Rozbetonowywanie: jak uprawiać warzywa i owoce w solarpunkowym mieście?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-depaving/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Question**: \n"
"Depaving: how to grow fruits and vegetables in the solarpunk city?\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pytanie**: \n"
"Rozbetonowywanie: jak uprawiać warzywa i owoce w solarpunkowym mieście?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-depaving/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Answer**:\n"
"Today cities are crammed with parking lots, multi-lane speedways, garages and gas stations.\n"
"What will happen to these toxic relics of the past in the solarpunk city?\n"
"They will be reclaimed and returned to the community!\n"
msgstr ""
"**Odpowiedź po angielsku**:\n"
"Today cities are crammed with parking lots, multi-lane speedways, garages and gas stations.\n"
"What will happen to these toxic relics of the past in the solarpunk city?\n"
"They will be reclaimed and returned to the community!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-depaving/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Residents band together in self-organized work teams and, with the help of "
"crowbars and pickaxes, rip out the tarmac, revealing the ground underneath.  "
"Gardeners, permaculture experts and rewilders rush in with cartloads of "
"compost, donated by the neighbours and turn non-places into gardens, "
"allotments and biodiverse habitats for invertebrates, birds and small "
"mammals.  Even the fuel tanks of the gas stations can be reused, once "
"reclaimed. Now they are water reservoirs for the dry season, which fill up "
"slowly during autumn and winter thanks to water harvesting systems."
msgstr ""
"Residents band together in self-organized work teams and, with the help of "
"crowbars and pickaxes, rip out the tarmac, revealing the ground underneath.  "
"Gardeners, permaculture experts and rewilders rush in with cartloads of "
"compost, donated by the neighbours and turn non-places into gardens, "
"allotments and biodiverse habitats for invertebrates, birds and small "
"mammals.  Even the fuel tanks of the gas stations can be reused, once "
"reclaimed. Now they are water reservoirs for the dry season, which fill up "
"slowly during autumn and winter thanks to water harvesting systems."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-depaving/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Where only cars dared to roll, now there is a pocket meadow, or a food "
"forest, or an allotment where the neighbours can plant local, healthy food.  "
"Nearby, a group of young volunteers are climbing on a van (electric, with "
"sodium batteries) from the Rewilding Guild. They are off to depave most of "
"the lanes of the A1 motorway, now almost disused, and turn it into Europe's "
"longest linear park.  But fear not! There are enough paved surfaces for "
"bicycles, wheelchairs, baby strollers, scooters and pedestrians, and even "
"for the few cars and vans still in use."
msgstr ""
"Where only cars dared to roll, now there is a pocket meadow, or a food "
"forest, or an allotment where the neighbours can plant local, healthy food.  "
"Nearby, a group of young volunteers are climbing on a van (electric, with "
"sodium batteries) from the Rewilding Guild. They are off to depave most of "
"the lanes of the A1 motorway, now almost disused, and turn it into Europe's "
"longest linear park.  But fear not! There are enough paved surfaces for "
"bicycles, wheelchairs, baby strollers, scooters and pedestrians, and even "
"for the few cars and vans still in use."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-depaving/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The difference is that now cities are no longer built around cars: they are "
"merely guests."
msgstr ""
"The difference is that now cities are no longer built around cars: they are "
"merely guests."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-federated-grid/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is a Federated Grid?"
msgstr "Czym jest zdystrybuowana sieć elektryczna?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-federated-grid/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Question**: \n"
"What is a Federated Grid?\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pytanie**: \n"
"Czym jest zdystrybuowana sieć elektryczna?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-federated-grid/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Answer**:\n"
"What happens to the solarpunk city when the energy grid is hit by an adverse weather event or another natural disaster?\n"
"To make a long story very short: not a lot.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Odpowiedź po angielsku**:\n"
"What happens to the solarpunk city when the energy grid is hit by an adverse weather event or another natural disaster?\n"
"To make a long story very short: not a lot.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-federated-grid/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The solarpunk society has learned its lesson from the mistakes of the Late "
"Stage Capitalism (week-long blackouts, no service for months in some cases) "
"and completely redesigned its approach to energy provisioning.  As for "
"communications, there is no longer a National Grid, but rather a Federated "
"Grid.  Inspired by Nature, the Federated Grid is fractal. Every "
"neighbourhood, village or cluster of houses has its own grid, where everyone "
"is both a producer and a consumer, and these networks are connected together "
"within a region, and then again within a bioregion, and so on and so forth. "
"And the best thing is that neighbouring networks can help each other, should "
"something happen."
msgstr ""
"The solarpunk society has learned its lesson from the mistakes of the Late "
"Stage (week-long blackouts, no service for months in some cases) and "
"completely redesigned its approach to energy provisioning.  As for "
"communications, there is no longer a National Grid, but rather a Federated "
"Grid.  Inspired by Nature, the Federated Grid is fractal. Every "
"neighbourhood, village or cluster of houses has its own grid, where everyone "
"is both a producer and a consumer, and these networks are connected together "
"within a region, and then again within a bioregion, and so on and so forth. "
"And the best thing is that neighbouring networks can help each other, should "
"something happen."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-federated-grid/index.en.md
msgid ""
"A freak hailstorm has damaged the solar panels? A winter storm has toppled a "
"wind farm? An earthquake has taken down the high tension lines? Neighbouring "
"networks take over until repairs are completed, and it takes a lot less than "
"it used to. Most people have at least some training on the maintenance of "
"solar implants or domestic wind turbines, and special Energy Sovereignty "
"Groups are at hand to tackle more complex cases.  There are no more b******s "
"who laugh at the phone thinking about how much money they can profit off the "
"reconstruction, nor decades-long odysseys of families stuck in prefabs, nor "
"regions fighting against each other for resources.  The solarpunk society "
"learned that faced with the consequences of the foolishness of the Late "
"Stage, or the imperatives of Nature, the only sensible responses are "
"solidarity and collaboration."
msgstr ""
"A freak hailstorm has damaged the solar panels? A winter storm has toppled a "
"wind farm? An earthquake has taken down the high tension lines? Neighbouring "
"networks take over until repairs are completed, and it takes a lot less than "
"it used to. Most people have at least some training on the maintenance of "
"solar implants or domestic wind turbines, and special Energy Sovereignty "
"Groups are at hand to tackle more complex cases.  There are no more b******s "
"who laugh at the phone thinking about how much money they can profit off the "
"reconstruction, nor decades-long odysseys of families stuck in prefabs, nor "
"regions fighting against each other for resources.  The solarpunk society "
"learned that faced with the consequences of the foolishness of the Late "
"Stage, or the imperatives of Nature, the only sensible responses are "
"solidarity and collaboration."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-goods-exchange/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "How does a solarpunk city exchange goods?"
msgstr "Jak solarpunkowe miasto wymienia się dobrami?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-goods-exchange/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Question**: \n"
"How does a solarpunk city exchange goods with other solarpunk communities across the globe?\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pytanie**: \n"
"Jak solarpunkowe miasto wymienia się dobrami z innymi społecznościami dookoła świata?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-goods-exchange/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Answer**:\n"
"The members of an Ethical Purchasing Group (EPG) get their heads together and send a purchase request directly to consortia of small producers, who prepare the orders and get in touch with transport cooperatives for shipment. Federated platforms help EPGs and producers to keep in touch and plan regular and ad-hoc shipments in the most effective and efficient way. Sailing ships, traditionally built or high-tech, ply the routes of the Mediterranean, hopping from port to port to load and unload all sorts of goods. They belong to cooperatives who collect shipments directly from local producers. Once in port, the crews unload the goods on cargo trains which carry them towards regional exchange centres and cargo railyards. \n"
msgstr ""
"**Odpowiedź po angielsku**:\n"
"The members of an Ethical Purchasing Group (EPG) get their heads together and send a purchase request directly to consortia of small producers, who prepare the orders and get in touch with transport cooperatives for shipment. Federated platforms help EPGs and producers to keep in touch and plan regular and ad-hoc shipments in the most effective and efficient way. Sailing ships, traditionally built or high-tech, ply the routes of the Mediterranean, hopping from port to port to load and unload all sorts of goods. They belong to cooperatives who collect shipments directly from local producers. Once in port, the crews unload the goods on cargo trains which carry them towards regional exchange centres and cargo railyards. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-goods-exchange/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Here, local cooperatives load them on cargo filobus, which use green energy "
"directly from the federated mains to carry them to various neighbourhoods, "
"towns and villages on their route. Delegates from the EPGs go fetch their "
"purchases from designated cargo bus stops, on their cargo bikes, electric or "
"not, or with carts, wheelbarrows and whatever else is at hand, and bring "
"them to the EPG meeting hall, where they are distributed among all members. "
"In turn, local producers hand over their goods to the transport "
"cooperatives, so that they can start their trip in the reverse direction "
"towards communities near and far.  Exchanges are planned to be fair and "
"equal from the outset."
msgstr ""
"Here, local cooperatives load them on cargo filobus, which use green energy "
"directly from the federated mains to carry them to various neighbourhoods, "
"towns and villages on their route. Delegates from the EPGs go fetch their "
"purchases from designated cargo bus stops, on their cargo bikes, electric or "
"not, or with carts, wheelbarrows and whatever else is at hand, and bring "
"them to the EPG meeting hall, where they are distributed among all members. "
"In turn, local producers hand over their goods to the transport "
"cooperatives, so that they can start their trip in the reverse direction "
"towards communities near and far.  Exchanges are planned to be fair and "
"equal from the outset."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-how-do-people-move-around/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "How do people move around the solarpunk city?"
msgstr "Jak ludzie poruszają się po solarpunkowym mieście?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-how-do-people-move-around/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Question**: \n"
"How do people move around the solarpunk city?\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pytanie**: \n"
"Jak ludzie poruszają się po solarpunkowym mieście?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-how-do-people-move-around/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Answer**: \n"
"With public transportation which has been enormously expanded. Private transportation is mostly limited to adapted vehicles for special mobility needs, and vehicles are available through shared ownership schemes.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Odpowiedź po angielsku**: \n"
"With public transportation which has been enormously expanded. Private transportation is mostly limited to adapted vehicles for special mobility needs, and vehicles are available through shared ownership schemes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-how-do-people-move-around/index.en.md
msgid ""
"It is concert season in the solarpunk city and Webby has decided to go to "
"the Auditorium on her Isetta EV, specially adapted for people with her "
"mobility needs. It can be boarded through a ramp, and the steering, which "
"features an extra wheel to control brakes and accelerator,  can be moved out "
"of the way to allow Webby to board and disembark seamlessly. Strictly "
"speaking, the car is not just hers... It is part of a dedicated car-sharing "
"scheme, managed through a municipalized distributed ownership programme."
msgstr ""
"It is concert season in the solarpunk city and Webby has decided to go to "
"the Auditorium on her Isetta EV, specially adapted for people with her "
"mobility needs. It can be boarded through a ramp, and the steering, which "
"features an extra wheel to control brakes and accelerator,  can be moved out "
"of the way to allow Webby to board and disembark seamlessly. Strictly "
"speaking, the car is not just hers... It is part of a dedicated car-sharing "
"scheme, managed through a municipalized distributed ownership programme."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-how-do-people-move-around/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Next to her, Diego, a sight-impaired musician, follows the orange path "
"painted on the floor towards the Auditorium: the sensors in his next-gen "
"walking stick can tell him where to turn and how far it is."
msgstr ""
"Next to her, Diego, a sight-impaired musician, follows the orange path "
"painted on the floor towards the Auditorium: the sensors in his next-gen "
"walking stick can tell him where to turn and how far it is."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-human-artisan/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Human = Artisan"
msgstr "Człowiek = Rzemieślnik"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-human-artisan/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Topic**: \n"
"Human = Artisan\n"
msgstr ""
"**Temat**: \n"
"Człowiek = Rzemieślnik\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-human-artisan/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Description**:\n"
"The solarpunk society of the future also celebrates important festivities.\n"
"To tell the truth, people celebrate an even greater number of them.\n"
"Since frantic productivism has been abandoned, everybody has much more time to socialize and relax.\n"
"It is December now, and people get ready to celebrate a variety of festivals: Hanukkah, Yule, Christmas, Kwanzaa - the more, the merrier.\n"
"The solarpunk city is a hive of activity: some people decorate their houses and neighborhoods, some prepare enough food to feed a small army for the community banquets and, clearly, some think of the presents.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Opis po angielsku**:\n"
"The solarpunk society of the future also celebrates important festivities.\n"
"To tell the truth, people celebrate an even greater number of them.\n"
"Since frantic productivism has been abandoned, everybody has much more time to socialize and relax.\n"
"It is December now, and people get ready to celebrate a variety of festivals: Hanukkah, Yule, Christmas, Kwanzaa - the more, the merrier.\n"
"The solarpunk city is a hive of activity: some people decorate their houses and neighborhoods, some prepare enough food to feed a small army for the community banquets and, clearly, some think of the presents.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-human-artisan/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Unlike in the Late Stage, people don't feel pressured to show off by "
"spending tons of money to secure the latest gadgets and fashion. People take "
"their time to create something.  Here Ginny puts together a necklace for her "
"grandmother out of foraged material from the local woods. There, Marcello is "
"in the zone, spins some yarn while headbanging to power metal: a friend has "
"given him some wool from the commune's alpacas, and he wants to give it to "
"his boyfriend, a veritable knitting fiend.  Lori, instead, doesn't have much "
"talent for handcrafts, but for the best part of the year they have "
"accumulated LETS credits by looking after pets and children and modelling "
"for life drawing classes. Now they have enough to barter them with a "
"consortium of artisans and have them make a pair of Oleatex boots for their "
"little sister."
msgstr ""
"Unlike in the Late Stage, people don't feel pressured to show off by "
"spending tons of money to secure the latest gadgets and fashion. People take "
"their time to create something.  Here Ginny puts together a necklace for her "
"grandmother out of foraged material from the local woods. There, Marcello is "
"in the zone, spins some yarn while headbanging to power metal: a friend has "
"given him some wool from the commune's alpacas, and he wants to give it to "
"his boyfriend, a veritable knitting fiend.  Lori, instead, doesn't have much "
"talent for handcrafts, but for the best part of the year they have "
"accumulated LETS credits by looking after pets and children and modelling "
"for life drawing classes. Now they have enough to barter them with a "
"consortium of artisans and have them make a pair of Oleatex boots for their "
"little sister."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-human-artisan/index.en.md
msgid ""
"People have learned that who they are is not what they own or how much they "
"spend and that love shows better through time and care than through money.  "
"People celebrate and create leisurely, savouring the process as much as the "
"results."
msgstr ""
"People have learned that who they are is not what they own or how much they "
"spend and that love shows better through time and care than through money.  "
"People celebrate and create leisurely, savouring the process as much as the "
"results."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-sustainable-abundance/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sustainable abundance"
msgstr "Odżywalny dobrobyt"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-sustainable-abundance/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Topic**: \n"
"Sustainable abundance\n"
msgstr ""
"**Temat**: \n"
"Odżywalny dobrobyt\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-sustainable-abundance/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Description**:\n"
"Every year between April and November the solarpunk city is transformed. Flowers, fruits and crops of all sorts appear on balconies and terraces and community allotments, in flower beds and even on bush shelters sometimes. Maybe the city is not quite self-sufficient food-wise, and lives in strict symbiosis with the countryside that surrounds it, but during the right season it still gets hit with waves of abundance.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Opis po angielsku**:\n"
"Every year between April and November the solarpunk city is transformed. Flowers, fruits and crops of all sorts appear on balconies and terraces and community allotments, in flower beds and even on bush shelters sometimes. Maybe the city is not quite self-sufficient food-wise, and lives in strict symbiosis with the countryside that surrounds it, but during the right season it still gets hit with waves of abundance.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-sustainable-abundance/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The residents celebrate the fresh produce. They organize open-air feasts in "
"gardens and orchards, centred on strawberries, tomatoes or courgettes, each "
"in its season, but for the most part there is more fresh food that can be "
"consumed, even through repeated parties.  The residents then gather again in "
"the community centres of each neighbourhood and pull out pressure cookers, "
"autoclaves, drying lattices and driers, and a truly astonishing quantity of "
"glass jars, and work together for days on end, sometimes weeks, turning that "
"cornucopia into jams, preserves and conserves of all kind.  Garlic braids, "
"chili garlands and dried tomato mosaics, laid out on lattices adorn every "
"building, and the shelves of the community pantries groan under the weight "
"of hundreds of glass jars, all duly labelled.  All around educators and "
"childcare volunteers help the young ones take part in the proceedings, or "
"keep them occupied while their adults work.  Someone even plays the guitar "
"to entertain the workers. It is basically a party all over again.  Nearby a "
"group of fiber artists uses peels, seeds and other off-cuts to make pigments "
"and dye yarn made from hemp, flax and nettles.  Compost piles grow taller "
"and fatter with new material. By the time Spring comes around again, it will "
"be ready to nurture new harvests."
msgstr ""
"The residents celebrate the fresh produce. They organize open-air feasts in "
"gardens and orchards, centred on strawberries, tomatoes or courgettes, each "
"in its season, but for the most part there is more fresh food that can be "
"consumed, even through repeated parties.  The residents then gather again in "
"the community centres of each neighbourhood and pull out pressure cookers, "
"autoclaves, drying lattices and driers, and a truly astonishing quantity of "
"glass jars, and work together for days on end, sometimes weeks, turning that "
"cornucopia into jams, preserves and conserves of all kind.  Garlic braids, "
"chili garlands and dried tomato mosaics, laid out on lattices adorn every "
"building, and the shelves of the community pantries groan under the weight "
"of hundreds of glass jars, all duly labelled.  All around educators and "
"childcare volunteers help the young ones take part in the proceedings, or "
"keep them occupied while their adults work.  Someone even plays the guitar "
"to entertain the workers. It is basically a party all over again.  Nearby a "
"group of fiber artists uses peels, seeds and other off-cuts to make pigments "
"and dye yarn made from hemp, flax and nettles.  Compost piles grow taller "
"and fatter with new material. By the time Spring comes around again, it will "
"be ready to nurture new harvests."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-sustainable-abundance/index.en.md
msgid ""
"In the solarpunk city abundance is never wasted, it is shared with everyone."
msgstr ""
"In the solarpunk city abundance is never wasted, it is shared with everyone."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-sustainable-mobility/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "What does sustainable mobility mean in the solarpunk city?"
msgstr "Czym jest odżywalny transport w solarpunkowym mieście?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-sustainable-mobility/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Question**: \n"
"What does sustainable mobility mean in the solarpunk city?\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pytanie**: \n"
"Czym jest odżywalny transport w solarpunkowym mieście?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-sustainable-mobility/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Answer**:\n"
"In the solarpunk city, private cars have become an exception rather than the rule, and their numbers no longer justify the spaces they had taken. The citizens transform parking lots, junctions and roads into spaces for nature and community. In Milan, the people re-open the Navigli and the other canals which had made the city prosper in the Middle Ages and which had been covered in the 50s and 60s to make space for cars.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Odpowiedź po angielsku**:\n"
"In the solarpunk city, private cars have become an exception rather than the rule, and their numbers no longer justify the spaces they had taken. The citizens transform parking lots, junctions and roads into spaces for nature and community. In Milan, the people re-open the Navigli and the other canals which had made the city prosper in the Middle Ages and which had been covered in the 50s and 60s to make space for cars.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-sustainable-mobility/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Emys Orbicularis is a solar-powered water bus. She is named after one of the "
"species of freshwater turtles that can be found in Italy, with which she "
"shares a certain resemblance because of its shell, made of solar panels. "
"Water buses like this ply the waters, bringing travellers, workers and "
"students across the city. With a little bit of patience, one can get to "
"Pavia, the Lakes and the Po, on a boat or along the long-distance cycle "
"paths, fully equipped to welcome all travellers."
msgstr ""
"Emys Orbicularis is a solar-powered water bus. She is named after one of the "
"species of freshwater turtles that can be found in Italy, with which she "
"shares a certain resemblance because of its shell, made of solar panels. "
"Water buses like this ply the waters, bringing travellers, workers and "
"students across the city. With a little bit of patience, one can get to "
"Pavia, the Lakes and the Po, on a boat or along the long-distance cycle "
"paths, fully equipped to welcome all travellers."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-sustainable-mobility/index.en.md
msgid "People travel without haste, and without emissions."
msgstr "People travel without haste, and without emissions."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-symbiosis-energy-nature/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Symbiosis between energy and nature"
msgstr "Symbioza między energią a przyrodą"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-symbiosis-energy-nature/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Topic**: \n"
"Symbiosis between energy and nature\n"
msgstr ""
"**Temat**: \n"
"Symbioza między energią a przyrodą\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-symbiosis-energy-nature/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Description**:\n"
"Upon crossing the countryside surrounding the solarpunk city on a bike, a boat or a train, a visitor from our world would feel a bit disconcerted.\n"
"Where are the monocultures that once upon a time spread as far as the eye could see? And what are all those solar panels doing there? And most of all, who let the sheep out in the olive grove?\n"
msgstr ""
"**Opis po angielsku**:\n"
"Upon crossing the countryside surrounding the solarpunk city on a bike, a boat or a train, a visitor from our world would feel a bit disconcerted.\n"
"Where are the monocultures that once upon a time spread as far as the eye could see? And what are all those solar panels doing there? And most of all, who let the sheep out in the olive grove?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-symbiosis-energy-nature/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Agroecology techniques have replaced for the most part the industrial "
"agriculture paradigm of the Late Stage.  Fields are no longer \"flat "
"factories\" meant to extract resources, but fully realized eco-systems which "
"support biodiversity as well as human wellbeing.  Concepts like food forests "
"and agro-silvo-pastoralism are very popular, people talk about them at the "
"bar, as much as once they talked about the stock exchange.  Climate "
"adaptation has changed farmers' habits: some crops, no longer suitable to a "
"hotter, more extreme climate, have been abandoned, while others have been "
"introduced (bananas from Puglia and coffee from Sicily are now common "
"sights)."
msgstr ""
"Agroecology techniques have replaced for the most part the industrial "
"agriculture paradigm of the Late Stage.  Fields are no longer \"flat "
"factories\" meant to extract resources, but fully realized eco-systems which "
"support biodiversity as well as human wellbeing.  Concepts like food forests "
"and agro-silvo-pastoralism are very popular, people talk about them at the "
"bar, as much as once they talked about the stock exchange.  Climate "
"adaptation has changed farmers' habits: some crops, no longer suitable to a "
"hotter, more extreme climate, have been abandoned, while others have been "
"introduced (bananas from Puglia and coffee from Sicily are now common "
"sights)."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-symbiosis-energy-nature/index.en.md
msgid ""
"To protect their precious crops from the Sun, some farmers have converted to "
"agrosolar, installing solar panels between crop rows or shading the whole "
"field. Some of these covers have curious shapes: the solar panels are "
"arranged in a semi sphere.  Berries, salad leaves, citrus fruits and tea "
"(from Liguria, like pesto) are much happier, and rural communities have a "
"source of energetic sovereignty without having to sacrifice either Nature or "
"Agriculture."
msgstr ""
"To protect their precious crops from the Sun, some farmers have converted to "
"agrosolar, installing solar panels between crop rows or shading the whole "
"field. Some of these covers have curious shapes: the solar panels are "
"arranged in a semi sphere.  Berries, salad leaves, citrus fruits and tea "
"(from Liguria, like pesto) are much happier, and rural communities have a "
"source of energetic sovereignty without having to sacrifice either Nature or "
"Agriculture."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-symbiosis-energy-nature/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Now that profit is no longer the main decision-making factor, the solarpunk "
"world is full of creative and innovative solutions."
msgstr ""
"Now that profit is no longer the main decision-making factor, the solarpunk "
"world is full of creative and innovative solutions."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-the-factory/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Factory"
msgstr "Fabryka"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-the-factory/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Topic**: \n"
"The Factory\n"
msgstr ""
"**Temat**: \n"
"Fabryka\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-the-factory/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Description**:\n"
"In the solarpunk society there is a factory which doubles as a historic monument, whose story is taught in schools. In Italy the Just Transition, from the bottom up and mutualistic, started there. Abandoned by bosses and politicians after the latest industrial crisis, with the threat of redundancy over their heads, the workers occupied their factory and drew up an alternate industrial plan: out with car parts, in with cargo bikes and solar panels!\n"
"And in this postcard from the future of the factory we can see how the workers installed their new state-of-the-art solar panels: they are flexible and can adapt to the organic shapes obtained over a cluster of small wind turbines.\n"
"Zero-miles energy, from the Sun and from the wind.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Opis po angielsku**:\n"
"In the solarpunk society there is a factory which doubles as a historic monument, whose story is taught in schools. In Italy the Just Transition, from the bottom up and mutualistic, started there. Abandoned by bosses and politicians after the latest industrial crisis, with the threat of redundancy over their heads, the workers occupied their factory and drew up an alternate industrial plan: out with car parts, in with cargo bikes and solar panels!\n"
"And in this postcard from the future of the factory we can see how the workers installed their new state-of-the-art solar panels: they are flexible and can adapt to the organic shapes obtained over a cluster of small wind turbines.\n"
"Zero-miles energy, from the Sun and from the wind.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-the-factory/index.en.md
msgid ""
"With the help of activists and organizations, the workers gathered the "
"starting capital, set up a cooperative and got on with their plan. Following "
"their example, tens of other factories realized that they too could do "
"without bosses. Work for everyone, social value and a society wholly "
"transformed: together, workers and activists overturned the course of the "
"battle and won a better future for all of us."
msgstr ""
"With the help of activists and organizations, the workers gathered the "
"starting capital, set up a cooperative and got on with their plan. Following "
"their example, tens of other factories realized that they too could do "
"without bosses. Work for everyone, social value and a society wholly "
"transformed: together, workers and activists overturned the course of the "
"battle and won a better future for all of us."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-the-factory/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This sounds like it's a story from the future, but it is not: the GKN "
"Factory Collective needs your help right now to implement its Just "
"Transition plan. Read the full story and become a member of the cooperative "
"with a contribution at the website www.insorgiamo.org/100x10-000/"
msgstr ""
"This sounds like it's a story from the future, but it is not: the GKN "
"Factory Collective needs your help right now to implement its Just "
"Transition plan. Read the full story and become a member of the cooperative "
"with a contribution at the website www.insorgiamo.org/100x10-000/"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-the-factory/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Spread the word wherever people of conscience are.  Tomorrow's history is "
"made today: solarpunk is a verb for rising!"
msgstr ""
"Spread the word wherever people of conscience are.  Tomorrow's history is "
"made today: solarpunk is a verb for rising!"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-waste-or-resource/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Waste or resource?"
msgstr "Odpad czy surowiec?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-waste-or-resource/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Question**: \n"
"Waste or resource?\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pytanie**: \n"
"Odpad czy surowiec?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-waste-or-resource/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Answer**:\n"
"The insane production rhythms of the Late Stage are a thing of the past, but coffee remains one of the favourite beverages of the solarpunk city.\n"
"Its citizens meet for a chat over a cappuccino and a croissant, or discuss the management of the commons in their civic centres, helped along by thermoses of filter coffee and trays of food provided by the food sovereignty groups. Espresso, cappuccino, Turkish coffee, coffee masala, bubble coffee, and what have you, in the solarpunk city it is truly a transcultural phenomenon.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Odpowiedź po angielsku**:\n"
"The insane production rhythms of the Late Stage are a thing of the past, but coffee remains one of the favourite beverages of the solarpunk city.\n"
"Its citizens meet for a chat over a cappuccino and a croissant, or discuss the management of the commons in their civic centres, helped along by thermoses of filter coffee and trays of food provided by the food sovereignty groups. Espresso, cappuccino, Turkish coffee, coffee masala, bubble coffee, and what have you, in the solarpunk city it is truly a transcultural phenomenon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-waste-or-resource/index.en.md
msgid ""
"But what is to be done with the exhaust grounds? In the solarpunk city there "
"is no concept of waste or garbage. Everything is a resource that should be "
"used wisely to the benefit of nature and community.  Every day, teams of "
"workers from the local permaculture groups do the rounds of bars, "
"restaurants and community kitchens on their cargo bikes collecting food "
"scraps for their compost heaps. Since they have special uses, coffee and a "
"few other materials are collected separately, following a shared calendar "
"together with individual quotas and collection schemes to enable all "
"participants to benefit.  In the communal mushroom farms, built in the "
"basements of most condos throughout the city, experienced mushroom growers "
"from the food sovereignty groups use prodigious amounts of grounds as a "
"substrate for growing a cornucopia of different kinds of mushrooms to put on "
"the tables of their fellow citizens.  Eaten fresh in risottos and stir-frys, "
"dried or turned into vegan substitutes of bacon and jerky, mushrooms provide "
"sustainable, local protein for the solarpunk city, as well as construction "
"biomaterials, vegan leather and pharmaceuticals.  The humble coffee grounds, "
"useful for mushrooms and an incredible variety of other plants, are also a "
"load-bearing element of the city's sustainable strategy."
msgstr ""
"But what is to be done with the exhaust grounds? In the solarpunk city there "
"is no concept of waste or garbage. Everything is a resource that should be "
"used wisely to the benefit of nature and community.  Every day, teams of "
"workers from the local permaculture groups do the rounds of bars, "
"restaurants and community kitchens on their cargo bikes collecting food "
"scraps for their compost heaps. Since they have special uses, coffee and a "
"few other materials are collected separately, following a shared calendar "
"together with individual quotas and collection schemes to enable all "
"participants to benefit.  In the communal mushroom farms, built in the "
"basements of most condos throughout the city, experienced mushroom growers "
"from the food sovereignty groups use prodigious amounts of grounds as a "
"substrate for growing a cornucopia of different kinds of mushrooms to put on "
"the tables of their fellow citizens.  Eaten fresh in risottos and stir-frys, "
"dried or turned into vegan substitutes of bacon and jerky, mushrooms provide "
"sustainable, local protein for the solarpunk city, as well as construction "
"biomaterials, vegan leather and pharmaceuticals.  The humble coffee grounds, "
"useful for mushrooms and an incredible variety of other plants, are also a "
"load-bearing element of the city's sustainable strategy."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-water-management/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Water management, the solarpunk way"
msgstr "Gospodarka wodna w solarpunku"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-water-management/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Topic**: \n"
"Water management, the solarpunk way\n"
msgstr ""
"**Temat**: \n"
"Gospodarka wodna w solarpunku\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-water-management/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Description**:\n"
"Hard, impermeable surfaces have their uses, to allow bicycles, wheelchairs, strollers and yes, even the few surviving cars, all electric and with sodium batteries, to roll around undisturbed, but with weather patterns freely cycling between drought and torrential rain, the solarpunk city has had to transform, to become permeable and rethink its relationship with water.\n"
"Gardens and food growing spaces are designed around water harvesting and redirect the rain towards cisterns, ponds and other water reservoirs, which are used to water the plants in the try season. Drains and grey water pipes are directly connected to filtration systems. Used water is recovered and used again and again and again.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Opis po angielsku**:\n"
"Hard, impermeable surfaces have their uses, to allow bicycles, wheelchairs, strollers and yes, even the few surviving cars, all electric and with sodium batteries, to roll around undisturbed, but with weather patterns freely cycling between drought and torrential rain, the solarpunk city has had to transform, to become permeable and rethink its relationship with water.\n"
"Gardens and food growing spaces are designed around water harvesting and redirect the rain towards cisterns, ponds and other water reservoirs, which are used to water the plants in the try season. Drains and grey water pipes are directly connected to filtration systems. Used water is recovered and used again and again and again.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-water-management/index.en.md
msgid ""
"There is no need to worry about contamination from human waste. Excrement is "
"no longer dumped in the waterways like in the Late Stage, but are composted "
"into sterility and used for agriculture, a natural, endlessly renewable "
"fertilizer which has helped replace chemical fertilizers. Even urine has its "
"uses, as Vespasian said, and is employed as a mordant for dying and tanning "
"processes, or, diluted, as plant fertilizer."
msgstr ""
"There is no need to worry about contamination from human waste. Excrement is "
"no longer dumped in the waterways like in the Late Stage, but are composted "
"into sterility and used for agriculture, a natural, endlessly renewable "
"fertilizer which has helped replace chemical fertilizers. Even urine has its "
"uses, as Vespasian said, and is employed as a mordant for dying and tanning "
"processes, or, diluted, as plant fertilizer."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-water-management/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Low-lying skateparks become pools or ponds for part of the year, much to the "
"chagrin of skaters, who have to make do with SUP-ing and kayaking in the "
"newly reopened medieval canals or in the old seaplane landing strip. And "
"even there, they have to share their space with permaculturists: chinampas, "
"a traditional growing technique invented by the Aztecs which entails the "
"construction of floating islets of vegetation on which to grow crops or keep "
"poultry, have become extremely popular recently and dot most waterways.  In "
"Summer, when there is enough water, the residents flock to the re-forested "
"banks of the nearby rivers for a swim."
msgstr ""
"Low-lying skateparks become pools or ponds for part of the year, much to the "
"chagrin of skaters, who have to make do with SUP-ing and kayaking in the "
"newly reopened medieval canals or in the old seaplane landing strip. And "
"even there, they have to share their space with permaculturists: chinampas, "
"a traditional growing technique invented by the Aztecs which entails the "
"construction of floating islets of vegetation on which to grow crops or keep "
"poultry, have become extremely popular recently and dot most waterways.  In "
"Summer, when there is enough water, the residents flock to the re-forested "
"banks of the nearby rivers for a swim."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/panel-water-management/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Thanks to the drastic reduction in intensive animal agriculture and "
"industrial runoff, the waters are crystal clear and teeming with life: "
"dragonflies, frogs, fish, waterbirds, and even grass snakes which, though "
"harmless, never fail to cause a panic among the beachgoers.  The solarpunk "
"city has remembered that water is life and lives its life accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Thanks to the drastic reduction in intensive animal agriculture and "
"industrial runoff, the waters are crystal clear and teeming with life: "
"dragonflies, frogs, fish, waterbirds, and even grass snakes which, though "
"harmless, never fail to cause a panic among the beachgoers.  The solarpunk "
"city has remembered that water is life and lives its life accordingly."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/the-school-of-athens-2050/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The School of Athens 2050"
msgstr "Szkoła Ateńska 2050"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/the-school-of-athens-2050/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The School of Athens 2050 is a vision of a possible future. It was realized "
"for the spanish academic magazine of political ecology [Ecología Política]"
"(https://www.ecologiapolitica.info/), specifically for issue n°57 - [Las "
"Artes Y La Ecología Política](https://issuu.com/entmediambient/"
"docs/57_2019pkyxm), which focuses on the relationship between art and "
"political ecology."
msgstr ""
"Szkoła Ateństka 2050 to wizja możliwej przyszłości. Została stworzona dla "
"hiszpańskiego magazynu ekologii politycznej [Ecología Política](https://www."
"ecologiapolitica.info/), konkretnie do numeru 57go - [Las Artes Y La "
"Ecología Política](https://issuu.com/entmediambient/docs/57_2019pkyxm), "
"który skupia się na zależnościach między sztuką a ekologią polityczną."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/the-school-of-athens-2050/index.en.md
msgid ""
"In this case we imagined a new environment that is not rooted in any "
"specific location in the world, instead, since it collects people involved "
"with political ecology and art with different backgrounds from different "
"corners of the globe, it’s a place that can exist anywhere and that can "
"offer a sanctuary to each one of them."
msgstr ""
"W tym przypadku wyobraziliśmy sobie nowe środowisko, nie zakorzenione w "
"żadnym konkretnym miejscu na świecie, a zbierające ludzi związanych z "
"ekologią polityczną i sztuką z różnych dziedzin i zakątków świata. Może "
"przez to zaistnieć gdziekolwiek i stanowić sanktuarium dla każdego z nich."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/the-school-of-athens-2050/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The structure that covers the characters is a solar gazebo made of coloured "
"solar concentrators, a technology where panels are made of a semi-"
"transparent material that channel photons towards the mini silicon solar "
"panels that are installed on the sides of the concentrators. Usually the "
"coloured version of these panels are a by-product and are discarded, but in "
"this case we wanted to create a space that could spark ideas and boost "
"moods, so we decided to make it as colorful as we could. The structure that "
"sustains the panels would be made of recycled wooden beams, and the "
"buildings in the distance represent a new approach to architecture, more "
"connected with nature, hence the lotus and branches structures. In the "
"distance you can also see a floating wind turbine, suggesting the adoption "
"of a diffuse way of producing energy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/the-school-of-athens-2050/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The people are divided in several groups dedicated to different activities, "
"all sharing the same purpose of merging art, nature and tech. So in the "
"lower left corner we have the workshop of orange silk production, a new type "
"of textile fibre obtained by the manufacturing of the cellulose contained in "
"the orange peel. In this group of people you can see a lady using a portable "
"loom and [William Morris](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Morris), one "
"of the founders of the Arts and Crafts and of the Socialist movements in the "
"UK. He was also a writer, a publisher and an artist and in this composition "
"he is bringing to the workshop the oranges from his farm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/commando-jugendstil/the-school-of-athens-2050/index.en.md
msgid ""
"On the lower right corner there is the group working on 3D printing from "
"recycled plastic. Next to them, a rubbish collector droid brings some source "
"material to the group. Right above them there’s the group of activists, "
"which also takes all the rest of the higher level of the stage. Among them "
"you can see, from right to left: a reference to activist [Berta Cáceres]"
"(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berta_C%C3%A1ceres) and the pink boat that "
"took her name in the Extinction Rebellion protests in London, roman senator "
"[Lucio Sergio Catilina](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catiline), that was "
"demonized by the roman establishment and proposed agrarian reform and debt "
"jubilee, the founder of the movement of student strikes for climate [Greta "
"Thunberg](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greta_Thunberg), a member of the "
"[Standing Rock Sioux tribe](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Standing_Rock_Sioux_Reservation), battling to protect their land from oil "
"exploitation, and a member of the [Waorani Resistance](https://en.wikipedia."
"org/wiki/Waorani_people) in Ecuador, fighting to keep their land free from "
"oil drilling. The last three characters are inspired by famous painting [The "
"Fourth Estate](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fourth_Estate_(painting)), "
"by Pellizza da Volpedo, while the whole composition is a tribute to "
"masterpiece [The School of Athens](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"The_School_of_Athens) by [Raffaello](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raphael)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/cycling-embassy-japan/tokyo-pedals-forward/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tokyo Pedals Forward"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/cycling-embassy-japan/tokyo-pedals-forward/index.en.md
msgid "![Infographic version](./info.jpg)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/cycling-embassy-japan/tokyo-pedals-forward/index.en.md
msgid "[Interactive Link](https://cycling-embassy.jp/solarpunk/2026/)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/cycling-embassy-japan/tokyo-pedals-forward/index.en.md
msgid ""
"In this interactive artwork we explore how a city like Tokyo can strengthen "
"its disaster resilience through community participation, with bicycles "
"serving as a practical and accessible tool for post-disaster support."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/cycling-embassy-japan/tokyo-pedals-forward/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The composition is structured as a timeline, illustrating a progression from "
"present-day capabilities (left) to potential future innovations (right). It "
"highlights existing resources such as mobile communication devices and "
"conventional battery storage systems, while envisioning future developments "
"including micro-renewable energy technologies, fleets of electric emergency-"
"response bicycles, and rapidly deployable emergency shelters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/cycling-embassy-japan/tokyo-pedals-forward/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Together, these elements present a vision of a more resilient and self-"
"sufficient community, demonstrating how citizens, technology, and local "
"infrastructure can work together to support each other in the aftermath of a "
"disaster."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/back-home/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Back Home"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/back-home/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Even though I love cyberpunk aesthetic, it’s definitely not the kind of "
"society I’d want to live in. More and more often, when I look at the news, "
"it feels like we’re drifting toward a dystopia no one really wants, yet one "
"that seems inevitable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/back-home/index.en.md
msgid "But the truth is: nothing is inevitable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/back-home/index.en.md
msgid ""
"That’s why I’ve found myself increasingly imagining its exact opposite: "
"solarpunk. A world where cities coexist with nature, energy is clean and "
"renewable, and technology serves humanity instead of enslaving it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/back-home/index.en.md
msgid ""
"I love picturing small moments of everyday life in a world like that. It "
"makes me feel calmer, and a little more hopeful about the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/chilling-on-the-terrace/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chilling on the Terrace"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/chilling-on-the-terrace/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Like in almost all my illustrations, even when exploring the Solarpunk "
"genre, what I love most is imagining little everyday life moments like this "
"one. Just people unwinding after a long day, enjoying the evening breeze on "
"their terrace where they grow their own veggie garden."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/chilling-on-the-terrace/index.en.md
msgid ""
"I love the idea of bringing way more greenery into cities, along with "
"technology that's integrated with nature and produces clean, renewable "
"energy. The cool thing is that a future like this is already totally possible"
"—we just need the will to make it happen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/chilling-on-the-terrace/index.en.md
msgid ""
"I hope these illustrations bring you at least a bit of peace and hope for a "
"better future."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/community-aid-network/index.en.md
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "The Community Center"
msgid "Community Aid Network"
msgstr "Dom Kultury"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/community-aid-network/index.en.md
msgid ""
"A united, compassionate, and resilient community comes together in times of "
"crisis. A coordinated network of volunteers provides rescue efforts, medical "
"assistance, and warm meals to people displaced by an environmental disaster. "
"Everyone can contribute, even those without specialized training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/community-aid-network/index.en.md
msgid ""
"While it is wise not to rely entirely on technology, it can also play a "
"crucial role in managing critical situations by streamlining both physical "
"operations and organizational efforts, helping communities respond more "
"effectively when every moment counts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/community-aid-network/index.en.md
msgid ""
"But that's not all. Emotional support is just as important. When people feel "
"safe, protected, and supported by their community, they are more willing to "
"give back and help others in return, creating a positive cycle that benefits "
"everyone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/community-gardens/index.en.md
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "The Community Center"
msgid "Community Gardens"
msgstr "Dom Kultury"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/community-gardens/index.en.md
msgid ""
"I envisioned shared gardens within cities where anyone in the community can "
"plant and grow food freely, for everyone’s benefit, with the support of "
"solar-powered robots. Spaces to gather, connect, and spend some relaxing "
"time together, where workshops for children and other community activities "
"can also be organized. A service by the community, for the community."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/morning-sun/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Morning Sun"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/morning-sun/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Imagine waking up to a forest-city: a place with all the comforts of modern "
"life, powered by clean air, renewable energy, and technology designed to "
"cooperate with nature, not dominate it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/morning-sun/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Exploring Solarpunk reminds me that this future is not a fantasy. It’s "
"possible. But only if we stop treating the planet as something to control, "
"and start recognizing that we are part of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/solarpunk-cityscape/index.en.md
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Solarpunk City"
msgid "Solarpunk Cityscape"
msgstr "Solarpunkowe miasto"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/solarpunk-cityscape/index.en.md
msgid ""
"I think anyone who stumbles across the Solarpunk genre ends up asking the "
"same question: could a future like this really exist? A world where humans "
"live in true harmony with nature, and tech is here to help us—not control us?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/solarpunk-cityscape/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Even though today’s world feels more and more like a cyberpunk dystopia, my "
"answer to that question is still: yes, absolutely."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/solarpunk-cityscape/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Because honestly? We already have everything we need to build that kind of "
"future. We just need to start imagining it—more and more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/solarpunk-cityscape/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Taking action is super important, of course. But being able to imagine "
"something is the bare minimum if you ever want to make it real."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/daniele-turturici/solarpunk-cityscape/index.en.md
msgid "And art? Art is often the spark that sets change in motion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/deelion/neighbourhood-care/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Neighbourhood Care"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/deelion/neighbourhood-care/index.en.md
msgid ""
"It's the third flood in as many years, but these neighbours have built a "
"pretty resilient local system to prepare themselves."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/deelion/neighbourhood-care/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Basement apartment residents are boxing up their treasured memories and "
"preparing to catch the last community bus service across town, or for "
"sleepovers with their upstairs neighbours."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/deelion/neighbourhood-care/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Projector drones, equipped with latest forecasts, are followed around by the "
"local children brandishing chalk, marking up the walls so the sandbag teams "
"know how high to stack before moving onto the next house."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/deelion/neighbourhood-care/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The local communication network becomes a community aid message board, so "
"assistance is never far away, and since the shared tool sheds were built on "
"every street last year, responders can travel light and work fast."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/deelion/neighbourhood-care/index.en.md
msgid ""
"They've learned to rely on each other, and they know they'll be okay "
"because, as the graffitied old Neighbourhood Watch poster in the window "
"says: this neighbourhood cares."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/draakart/solarpunk-city-namaqualand/index.en.md
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Solarpunk City"
msgid "Solarpunk City Namaqualand"
msgstr "Solarpunkowe miasto"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/draakart/solarpunk-city-namaqualand/index.en.md
msgid "Submission for the 2023 Solarpunk City Art Collaboration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/draakart/solarpunk-city-namaqualand/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The bioregion depicted is the Deserts and Xeric Shrublands of Namaqualand, "
"South Africa, a desert famous for its unique ability to change from a dusty "
"wasteland into a very lush wildflower field after the first rains of spring. "
"This is set just after the rains."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/draakart/solarpunk-city-namaqualand/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The buildings featured are Ndebele-style homes, which are made of cob and "
"straw. They are excellent for the environment of South Africa and trap heat "
"in their walls during the very hot days and release this heat in the frigid "
"nights."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/draakart/solarpunk-city-namaqualand/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The city itself is connected by raised tramlines that traverse the landscape "
"in a web-like formation. All stations are within walking distance. The large "
"building in this painting is a library of some sort."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/draakart/solarpunk-city-namaqualand/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Some seasonal crops grown include pearl millet and cassava. The year-round "
"food sources are cattle, poultry, sour fig and groundnut. During dry spells, "
"where other crops fail, there are ample fruits from marula, sourplum and "
"monkey orange."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/draakart/solarpunk-city-namaqualand/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Drinking water is drawn up from wells using wind turbines, which, alongside "
"solarpanels, are the town's staple energy sources. The one depicted is "
"purely for pumping water, however.  The large dogs in the paintings are "
"Boerbols, which were traditionally used for lion hunting, but now act as "
"guardians, especially to the children. The smell of livestock is bound to "
"attract predators to the settlement, especially during lean times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/draakart/solarpunk-city-namaqualand/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The guinea fowl are companion animals to the chooks, acting as sentries."
msgstr ""

