#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/linds-brown/linden-street-aid-dock/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Linden Street Aid Dock"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/linds-brown/linden-street-aid-dock/index.en.md
msgid ""
"I wanted to show how my street could respond to a flood if one were to "
"happen tomorrow in my town in Louisiana, USA."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/linds-brown/linden-street-aid-dock/index.en.md
msgid ""
"On June 15, we experienced a lot of flooding in town and while the water did "
"not get as high as in my illustration it has made me think about how I will "
"need to work with neighbors to provide food, water, sandbags, a charging "
"station, a med station, a washing area, and of course, a social area."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/linds-brown/linden-street-aid-dock/index.en.md
msgid ""
"A lot of people where I live keep boats. I imagine people would float around "
"to help people and to go in search of aid."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/linds-brown/linden-street-aid-dock/index.en.md
msgid ""
"During Hurricaine Katrina in 2005, a number of people down south formed an "
"ad hoc group called, \"The Cajun Navy\" and worked outside (but sometimes "
"with) the government to help those in the flooding. The group has splintered "
"and some of the groups are non-profits now, but there is precedent for a "
"flotilla of Louisiana Solarpunks at some point in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/linds-brown/solar-cooking-class/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solar Cooking Class"
msgstr "Lekcja gotowania na kuchence słonecznej"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/linds-brown/solar-cooking-class/index.en.md
msgid ""
"[Original on Wikimedia Commons](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:"
"Solar_Cooking_Class_-_Solarpunk_Art_Collab_2025.jpg)"
msgstr ""
"[Oryginał na Wikimedia Commons](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:"
"Solar_Cooking_Class_-_Solarpunk_Art_Collab_2025.jpg)"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/linds-brown/solar-cooking-class/index.en.md
msgid ""
"For the theme, \"Life of Learning”, I wanted to show a solar cooking "
"demonstration held in an urban garden. For this demonstration, people are "
"totally free to come and go as they please, with no age-restrictions. In "
"addition to learning how the solar cooker works, the kids are also learning "
"how to identify herbs—especially really aggressive ones like peppermint that "
"make a fantastic tea and always needs thinning out. :)"
msgstr ""
"W ramach motywu \"Życia pełnego nauki\" chciałam pokazać demonstrację "
"kuchenki słonecznej w miejskim ogrodzie. Słuchacze mogą przyłączyć się - "
"albo pójść sobie - kiedy chcą, bez ograniczenia wieku. Oprócz dowiedzenia "
"się jak taka kuchenka działa, dzieci mogą też nauczyć się jak rozróżniać "
"zioła - szczególnie te bardziej agresywne, jak mięta, z której można zrobić "
"wspaniałą herbatę i którą zawsze dobrze wypielić. :)"

