#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/solhaelan/indy-lunarpunk/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Indy Lunarpunk"
msgstr "Indy Lunarpunk"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/solhaelan/indy-lunarpunk/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This piece imagines a near-future (or alternate-present) Indianapolis "
"without light pollution, where the illumination sources are all shifted "
"toward the red end of the spectrum to avoid the disruption of circadian "
"rythyms and chiropteran flight patterns, and where folk dance and sing under "
"the stars and the streetlights, which are made to look like Canada lilies "
"(Lilium canadense)."
msgstr ""
"This piece imagines a near-future (or alternate-present) Indianapolis "
"without light pollution, where the illumination sources are all shifted "
"toward the red end of the spectrum to avoid the disruption of circadian "
"rythyms and chiropteran flight patterns, and where folk dance and sing under "
"the stars and the streetlights, which are made to look like Canada lilies "
"(Lilium canadense)."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/solhaelan/knowledge-is-power/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Knowledge is Power"
msgstr "Wiedza to potęga"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/solhaelan/knowledge-is-power/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This Little Free Library (or Liberation Library, as the other term is "
"copyrighted) has a green roof with Echinacea purpurea (Purple Coneflower) "
"and Bignonia capreolata (Cross Vine) growing from it. It has a small "
"hexagonal solar panel powering string lights in the interior (red, for the "
"bats)."
msgstr ""
"This Little Free Library (or Liberation Library, as the other term is "
"copyrighted) has a green roof with Echinacea purpurea (Purple Coneflower) "
"and Bignonia capreolata (Cross Vine) growing from it. It has a small "
"hexagonal solar panel powering string lights in the interior (red, for the "
"bats)."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/solhaelan/suburban-rain-gardens/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suburban Rain Gardens"
msgstr "Deszczowe Ogrody Przedmieść"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/solhaelan/suburban-rain-gardens/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This digital painting depicts the Southern Great Lakes Ecoregion, within the "
"Interior Plateau & Southern Great Lakes Forests Bioregion, within the "
"Temperate Broadleaf and Mixed Forest Biome.  I chose a suburban setting for "
"this piece because I’ve not yet seen a Solarpunk artwork that features this. "
"I’m aware of the problems with the suburbs, but it seems to me more "
"sustainable to try to adapt them than to demolish them and start over. So "
"instead of lawns I’ve depicted beds of native Indiana plants, including but "
"not limited to:"
msgstr ""
"This digital painting depicts the Southern Great Lakes Ecoregion, within the "
"Interior Plateau & Southern Great Lakes Forests Bioregion, within the "
"Temperate Broadleaf and Mixed Forest Biome.  I chose a suburban setting for "
"this piece because I’ve not yet seen a Solarpunk artwork that features this. "
"I’m aware of the problems with the suburbs, but it seems to me more "
"sustainable to try to adapt them than to demolish them and start over. So "
"instead of lawns I’ve depicted beds of native Indiana plants, including but "
"not limited to:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/art/solhaelan/suburban-rain-gardens/index.en.md
msgid "Amsonia Tabernaemontana (Eastern Bluestar)"
msgstr "Amsonia Tabernaemontana (Eastern Bluestar)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/art/solhaelan/suburban-rain-gardens/index.en.md
msgid "Spartina Pectinata (Prairie Cordgrass)"
msgstr "Spartina Pectinata (Prairie Cordgrass)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/art/solhaelan/suburban-rain-gardens/index.en.md
msgid "Echinacea Purpurea (Purple Coneflower)."
msgstr "Echinacea Purpurea (Purple Coneflower)."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/solhaelan/suburban-rain-gardens/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The roofs of the houses are either white to help reflect heat, or green "
"roofs. Some of the houses are equipped with solar panels on the south sides, "
"and one is shown with a greenhouse on that side as well."
msgstr ""
"The roofs of the houses are either white to help reflect heat, or green "
"roofs. Some of the houses are equipped with solar panels on the south sides, "
"and one is shown with a greenhouse on that side as well."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/solhaelan/suburban-rain-gardens/index.en.md
msgid ""
"While perhaps not explicitly ecologically focused, I have shown there to be "
"more art in this setting than is usually found in american suburbia. The "
"sidewalk has a mural painted with hydrochromic paint, which only appears "
"while it is raining. The houses are painted bright colors (white or greige "
"is  considered ‘Normal’ ) and are occasionally decorated with murals."
msgstr ""
"While perhaps not explicitly ecologically focused, I have shown there to be "
"more art in this setting than is usually found in american suburbia. The "
"sidewalk has a mural painted with hydrochromic paint, which only appears "
"while it is raining. The houses are painted bright colors (white or greige "
"is  considered ‘Normal’ ) and are occasionally decorated with murals."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/solhaelan/suburban-rain-gardens/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This particular area is among the cloudiest in the so-called U.S.A. To "
"reflect that, the weather is overcast and it is currently raining."
msgstr ""
"This particular area is among the cloudiest in the so-called U.S.A. To "
"reflect that, the weather is overcast and it is currently raining."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/stephani-soejono/the-sunday-scene/index.en.md
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "The Community Center"
msgid "The Sunday Scene"
msgstr "Dom Kultury"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/stephani-soejono/the-sunday-scene/index.en.md
msgid ""
"I can feel the wind blowing through despite the heat. The mangoes are "
"starting to ripen too. Kang Asep has come all the way from the mountains of "
"Banten to trade his vegetables with our garden’s crop of snake fruits. My "
"daughter is having a blast showing her friend the new pollinator-friendly "
"hybrid flowers we are developing. I’ve asked Koh Aling to make Kang Asep and "
"his daughter fried rice for lunch. I hope we can re-pave the road sooner, "
"the weeds sometimes get stuck on my wheelchair. It’s a beautiful Sunday and "
"I am glad to be alive right now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/art/stephani-soejono/the-sunday-scene/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Illustrator Notes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/stephani-soejono/the-sunday-scene/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This piece takes quite a while to finish, partially my fault and partially "
"unexpected drawing tablet blowup. I started gardening too and that’s why I "
"drew the hibiscuses. I love hibiscus flowers.  I wanted to depict a "
"Solarpunk future that is specific to my region, Jakarta, Indonesia, South "
"East Asia. I based this market/urban garden off an area where people hung "
"out a lot. I quite like the way it is set up in a circle.  As you can see, "
"there is a roof that also doubles as a solar panel. In the centre there is a "
"mango tree complete with an explanation plaque with braille and regular "
"letters. As for the food stalls, I want it to be a compilation of my "
"favourite jajan pasar (market snacks). Starting with a fried rice/char kway "
"teow stall, classic Chinese-Indonesian food, savoury, spicy and smoky, "
"followed by es campur, shaved ice with mixed fruits and a hint of syrup, "
"perfect for a hot day, then towards toko kue, baked goods, serving "
"traditional cakes like kue lapis, but also stuff like croissants and ending "
"with batagor, fried fish cakes in peanut sauce. There is also a grass jelly "
"climbing plant next to the shaved ice stall, because I imagine if you can "
"get it as fresh as you can? Why not?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/stephani-soejono/the-sunday-scene/index.en.md
msgid ""
"I specifically focused on a single disabled mom and her daughrer and Kanekes "
"people for a few reasons. We in Jakarta have often failed disabled people - "
"and I want to imagine a future where they can live with dignity. The Kanekes "
"are indigenous people living in the Banten province and they still live off "
"grid. I want to imagine a future where we live - not entirely off grid but "
"adopting some of their ways so the earth can breathe a little easier. I hope "
"I get to see more location specific Solarpunk soon!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/redwood-highrise/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Redwood Highrise"
msgstr "Wieżowce wśród sekwoi"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/redwood-highrise/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Future: Dotted throughout a valley in the wild-urban interface of the Santa "
"Cruz Mountains, are pods of high-rise buildings, blending homes, businesses, "
"and community spaces. Tile mosaic murals lend the buildings extra protection "
"against stray embers from regular controlled burns on the forest floor. "
"Between the structures, rows of hydroponic crops hang, while pumpkin vines "
"climb sculptural trellises. Wildlife moves freely among the human "
"infrastructure. The community manages and harvests the forest’s mushrooms, "
"deer, salmon and herbs in a way that honors Indigenous people’s knowledge "
"and access to the land. Accessible walking paths meander through the valley, "
"supplemented by a gondola system for transporting goods and passengers "
"between pods. Select redwoods have been nurtured back to an old growth "
"state, sequestering carbon and fostering a cool, wet micro-climate. The "
"community’s decision to structure their forest home vertically mirrors the "
"epiphyte ecosystem on the redwood canopy."
msgstr ""
"Przyszłość: W dolinie położonej na styku dzikiej przyrody i miejskiej "
"zabudowy w górach Santa Cruz rozsiane są grupy wieżowców, łączące "
"mieszkania, przestrzenie społeczne i komercyjne. Mozaikowe murale z płytek "
"zapewniają budynkom dodatkową ochronę przed iskrami pochodzącymi z "
"regularnych kontrolowanych pożarów poszycia lasu. Pomiędzy budynkami wiszą "
"rzędy upraw hydroponicznych, a pnącza dyni wspinają się po rzeźbionych "
"kratach. Dzika przyroda porusza się swobodnie wśród infrastruktury "
"stworzonej przez człowieka. Społeczność zarządza lasem i zbiera grzyby, "
"poluje na jelenie, łowi łososie i zbiera zioła w sposób odzwierciedlające "
"wiedzę, zwyczaje i poszanowanie do ziemi rodzimych mieszkańców. Przez dolinę "
"wiją się dostępne ścieżki spacerowe, uzupełnione systemem gondoli do "
"transportu towarów i pasażerów między osiedlami. Wybrane sekwoje zostały "
"przywrócone do stanu pierwotnego, pochłaniając dwutlenek węgla i sprzyjając "
"chłodnemu, wilgotnemu mikroklimatowi. Decyzja społeczności o pionowej "
"strukturze swojego leśnego domu odzwierciedla ekosystem epifitów na koronach "
"sekwoi."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/san-francisco-civic-center/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "San Francisco's Civic Center"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/san-francisco-civic-center/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Present**: \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/san-francisco-civic-center/index.en.md
msgid ""
"During the City Beautiful Movement at the turn of the 20th century, city "
"planners used classical architecture to romanticize the **imperialistic "
"military ambitions of San Francisco’s wealthiest 1%**, all of whom were "
"heavily invested in the arms industry. San Francisco's City Hall and Civic "
"Center were focal points for this architectural movement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/san-francisco-civic-center/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Today, the suffering caused by wealth disparity is evident everywhere in San "
"Francisco, and not least in Civic Center, where many people make their lives "
"on the streets. This painting highlights elements of hostile architecture "
"and policy observed in the area: **surveillance cameras (foreground), "
"speakers that play Disney music at all hours (mounted on the light post on "
"the right), the lack of benches, and security guards tasked with preventing "
"people from lying down**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/san-francisco-civic-center/index.en.md
msgid ""
"From left to right: a security guard checks on someone who won’t immediately "
"sit up, a person sits after being told to do so and makes the best of the "
"moment by drawing in a sketch book, a custodian takes a break, a man watches "
"over his partner experiencing withdrawal, and three friends discuss politics "
"while sorting through their belongings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/san-francisco-civic-center/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Observed and painted en plein air. Inspired by *Imperial San Francisco*, by "
"Gray Brechin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/san-francisco-civic-center/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Future**: \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/san-francisco-civic-center/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "**City Hall has been repurposed as a co-created community space**. Its formerly bare walls and columns are decorated by artists who tell a people’s history of the city and extol the sacred values that inform the city’s future. During the Uprising, activists removed and repurposed the dome, viewing it as symbolic of hierarchy. Miraculously, a madrone took root at the base of the stairs in the central hall and grew up to burst out of the space of the former dome, becoming the tallest madrone ever on record. The roof now serves as a **transfer station for the gondola lines that criss-cross the city**. The building is still a beloved space for weddings and rites of passage. \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/san-francisco-civic-center/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Open and welcoming public spaces have returned to the city. In the "
"foreground is a public hammock space, alebrije statues, a native plant "
"garden, an adventure playground centered around a live oak tree, and a "
"preserved piece of the City Hall’s facade, which kids have painted on. The "
"kids play with fishing nets and invent ways to incorporate them into their "
"treehouse."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/san-francisco-civic-center/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This vision is inspired by The Fifth Sacred Thing by Starhawk and dreamed in "
"collaboration with local resident, writer, and activist Beverly Litkin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/traffic-rebellion/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Traffic Rebellion"
msgstr "Rebelia drogowa"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/traffic-rebellion/index.en.md
msgid ""
"On the left is a plein air painting of evening traffic as viewed from the "
"Morrissey Blvd overpass. On the right is a speculative repaint of our future "
"society. Shown is the Hwy 1 High Speed Rail at the center divider beside a "
"transfer station to the prolific local bus line. A line of native trees "
"divides the road from the rail. Through trial and error the community has "
"settled on a permit system allowing only occupational trucks to use the "
"roads with the busses. Vehicles are adorned with murals by local artists "
"instead of ads."
msgstr ""
"Po lewej widoczny jest plenerowy obraz ruchu drogowego widocznego z wiaduktu "
"Morrissey Blvd. Po prawej - przemalowane wyobrażenie przyszłości naszego "
"społeczeństwa. Pokazuję stację przesiadkową z kolei wysokich prędkości Hwy 1 "
"na lokalną sieć autobusową. Linia rodzimych drzew oddziela drogę od torów. "
"Metodą prób i błędów lokalna społeczność stworzyła system pozwoleń "
"umożliwiający jedynie ciężarówkom służbowym na dzielenie drogi z autobusami. "
"Zamiast reklam pojazdy przyozdobione są muralami stworzonymi przez lokalnych "
"artystów."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/youth-center/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Youth Center"
msgstr "Centrum młodzieżowe"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/youth-center/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Future: A thriving youth center has taken form in this refurbished Victorian "
"house. Young visitors access mental-health, spiritual, and vocational "
"guidance, as well as mediation support interwoven with the community. "
"Ceanothus blooms in front of the house attracting monarch butterflies. The "
"roof is thatched in tule as a green building practice and to honor local "
"Indigenous knowledge."
msgstr ""
"Przyszłość: W odrestaurowanym wiktoriańskim domu powstało prężnie działające "
"centrum młodzieżowe. Młodzi goście mają dostęp do poradnictwa w zakresie "
"zdrowia psychicznego, duchowości i wyboru zawodu, a także wsparcia "
"mediacyjnego powiązanego ze społecznością lokalną. Przed domem kwitnie "
"ceanothus, przyciągając motyle monarchy. Dach pokryty jest strzechą z tule, "
"co stanowi przykład zielonego budownictwa i hołd dla lokalnej wiedzy "
"rdzennych mieszkańców."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/youth-center/index.en.md
msgid ""
"A grandmother is there harvesting oranges with her grandson preparing to "
"make a group dinner. Nearby, a boy monitors solar panels as a part of an "
"engineering project. In the foreground, a grinding stone sits beside a milpa "
"of corn, beans, and squash just beginning to sprout."
msgstr ""
"Babcia zbiera pomarańcze wraz z wnukiem, przygotowując się do wspólnej "
"kolacji. W pobliżu chłopiec monitoruje panele słoneczne w ramach projektu "
"inżynieryjnego. Na pierwszym planie obok milpy z kukurydzą, fasolą i dynią, "
"które dopiero zaczynają kiełkować, leży kamień młyński."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/taylor-seamount/youth-center/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Dreamed in collaboration with Edgar Ibarra, of [MILPA Collective](https://"
"milpacollective.org/) and is inspired by MILPA’s intention to create a Less "
"Restrictive Program (LRP) for incarcerated youth in Santa Cruz County."
msgstr ""
"Projekt powstał we współpracy z Edgarem Ibarrą z [MILPA Collective](https://"
"milpacollective.org/) i jest inspirowany zamiarem MILPA stworzenia programu "
"mniej restrykcyjnego (LRP) dla młodzieży przebywającej w więzieniach w "
"hrabstwie Santa Cruz."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/abandoned-prison/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Abandoned prison in New Spark"
msgstr "Porzucone więzienie w Nowej Iskrze"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/abandoned-prison/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> What to do with prisons no longer in use? Some places restructure them to serve a different purpose, others turn them into reminders of the cruelty of the past. This is sort of that. After being wrecked just a smidgeon, the place wasn't maintained, but left to the elements and the reckless - it's now an overgrown relic full of graffiti and murals, and regularly visited by those who aren't scared of decaying stairs and shaky railings. It's a bit controversial among local adults, some arguing it should be cleaned up, others that it's an appropriate bit of risk for the younglings who need a bit of danger to feel alive. Some might still be feeling nostalgic for the times they hung around these moss-covered walls.\n"
">\n"
"> New generations are taught about the historical meaning of the site. As a result, coming there often fills one with a sense of both dread and a desire to unleash, to bring freedom into a space that was built to take it away. Teens aren't known to be very respectful, but the atmosphere and local legends do force at least a slight change of attitude in the visitors.\n"
msgstr ""
"> What to do with prisons no longer in use? Some places restructure them to serve a different purpose, others turn them into reminders of the cruelty of the past. This is sort of that. After being wrecked just a smidgeon, the place wasn't maintained, but left to the elements and the reckless - it's now an overgrown relic full of graffiti and murals, and regularly visited by those who aren't scared of decaying stairs and shaky railings. It's a bit controversial among local adults, some arguing it should be cleaned up, others that it's an appropriate bit of risk for the younglings who need a bit of danger to feel alive. Some might still be feeling nostalgic for the times they hung around these moss-covered walls.\n"
">\n"
"> New generations are taught about the historical meaning of the site. As a result, coming there often fills one with a sense of both dread and a desire to unleash, to bring freedom into a space that was built to take it away. Teens aren't known to be very respectful, but the atmosphere and local legends do force at least a slight change of attitude in the visitors.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/abandoned-prison/index.en.md
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/youth-dorm/index.en.md
msgid "The illustration is set in a small fictional town of New Spark."
msgstr "The illustration is set in a small fictional town of New Spark."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/canteen/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Canteen"
msgstr "Stołówka"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/canteen/index.en.md
msgid ""
"An illustration to one of the Solarpunk Prompts episodes, [The Canteen]"
"(https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-canteen) "
"[[transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-"
"Canteen)]:"
msgstr ""
"Ilustracja do odcinka podcastu Solarpunk Prompts - [The Canteen](https://"
"podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-canteen) [[transkrypt]"
"(https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Canteen)]:"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/canteen/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A canteen in an isolated scientific or environmental outpost, where scientists, engineers, cooks and maintenance staff show each other their human face, while still remembering the importance of their role here and the harsh conditions of the outside. For example: cleaning the plastic from the oceans, measuring the polar ice levels, etc.\n"
msgstr "> Stołówka w odizolowanej placówce naukowej / środowiskowej, gdzie naukowcy, inżynierowie, kucharze i pracownicy obsługi pokazują sobie nawzajem swoje ludzkie oblicze, jednocześnie pamiętając o tym, jak ważna jest ich rola tutaj i jak trudne warunki panują na zewnątrz (np. czyszczenie oceanów z plastiku, mierzenie poziomu lodu na biegunie północnym itp.).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/canteen/index.en.md
msgid "Based on the [story seed](/seeds/the-canteen)."
msgstr "Na podstawie [zalążka opowieści](/pl/seeds/the-canteen)."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/chefs/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Chefs"
msgstr "Kucharze"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/chefs/index.en.md
msgid ""
"An illustration to one of the Solarpunk Prompts episodes, [The Chefs]"
"(https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-chefs) "
"[[transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-"
"Chefs)]:"
msgstr ""
"Ilustracja do odcinka podcastu Solarpunk Prompts - [The Chefs](https://"
"podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-chefs) [[transkrypt]"
"(https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Chefs)]:"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/chefs/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A group of cooks, dietitians, and teachers are tasked with both creating and promoting well-rounded and tasty vegetarian cuisine in a world living through the culture shock of no affordable meat.\n"
msgstr "> Grupa kucharzy, dietetyków i nauczycieli, których zadaniem jest tworzenie i promowanie dobrze dopracowanej i smacznej kuchni wegańskiej/wegetariańskiej w świecie przeżywającym szok kulturowy związany z brakiem niedrogiego mięsa. Czy uda im się powstrzymać masową panikę i zamieszki?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/chefs/index.en.md
msgid "Based on the [story seed](/seeds/the-chefs)."
msgstr "Na podstawie [zalążka opowieści](/pl/seeds/the-chefs)."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/community-center/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Community Center"
msgstr "Dom Kultury"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/community-center/index.en.md
msgid ""
"An illustration to one of the Solarpunk Prompts episodes, [The Community "
"Center](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-"
"community-center) [[transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-"
"Prompts---The-Community-Center)]:"
msgstr ""
"Ilustracja do odcinka podcastu Solarpunk Prompts, [The Community Center]"
"(https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-community-"
"center) [[transkrypt](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---"
"The-Community-Center)]:"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/community-center/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A community center, library, or educational hub, initially set up to help people like coal miners re-specialize and find other jobs, has now became a place for unofficial “pilgrimages” of people striving to find their role in life and learn history from those who lived it.\n"
msgstr "> Dom kultury / biblioteka / ośrodek edukacyjny, początkowo założony, by pomóc ludziom takim jak górnicy w zdobyciu nowych umiejętności i znalezieniu innej pracy, teraz stał się miejscem nieoficjalnych „pielgrzymek” ludzi dążących do odnalezienia swojej roli w życiu i poznania historii od tych, którzy taką przemianę przeżyli.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/community-center/index.en.md
msgid "Based on the [story seed](/seeds/the-community-center)."
msgstr "Na podstawie [zalążka opowieści](/pl/seeds/the-community-center)."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/hackerspace/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "A prosthesis maintenance day at the hackerspace"
msgstr "Dzień naprawy protez w hakerspejsie"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/hackerspace/index.en.md
msgid ""
"An illustration for two separate Solarpunk Prompts episodes, [The Disabled "
"Community](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-"
"disabled-community) [[transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/"
"Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Disabled-Community)] and [The Hackerspace](https://"
"podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-hackerspace) "
"[[transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-"
"Hackerspace)]. Two halves representing the cover arts for each of the "
"episodes connect in the wider version above."
msgstr ""
"Ilustracja do dwóch oddzielnych odcinków podcastu Solarpunk Prompts - [The "
"Disabled Community](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/"
"the-disabled-community) [[transkrypt](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/"
"Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Disabled-Community)] i [The Hackerspace](https://"
"podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-hackerspace) "
"[[transkrypt](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-"
"Hackerspace)]. Dwie połówki będące okładkami każdego z nich łączą się w "
"szerszą wersję - powyżej."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/hackerspace/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A community of people with disabilities share their best tricks on how to deal with a harsh world not made for them. A lot of what they share remains unspoken, for every one knows the pain and the challenges they face.\n"
msgstr "> Społeczność osób z niepełnosprawnościami dzieli się najlepszymi sztuczkami, jak radzić sobie w trudnym świecie, który nie został dla nich stworzony. Wiele z tego, czym się dzielą, pozostaje niewypowiedziane, bo każdy z nich zna ból i wyzwania, z jakimi się mierzą.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/hackerspace/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A hackerspace sits within a city still clinging to their own ways while the rest of the world changes. Activists, technologists, inventors and educators trying to show the communities around them that it’s possible to live differently, while actively squabbling over whose plan is the best.\n"
msgstr "> Squat / hackerspace w mieście, które wciąż trzyma się starych schematów, podczas gdy reszta świata się zmienia. Aktywiści, technolodzy, wynalazcy i edukatorzy próbują pokazać społecznościom wokół siebie, że można żyć inaczej, a jednocześnie aktywnie spierają się o to, czyj plan jest najlepszy.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/hackerspace/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Based on the story seeds: [the hackerspace](/seeds/the-hackerspace) and [the "
"disabled community](/seeds/the-disabled-community)."
msgstr ""
"Na podstawie dwóch Zalążków Opowieści: [hackerspace](/pl/seeds/the-"
"hackerspace) i [niepełnosprawnych](/pl/seeds/the-disabled-community)."

