#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/rehearsal-at-portal/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rehearsal at Portal"
msgstr "Próba w Portalu"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/rehearsal-at-portal/index.en.md
msgid ""
"For this, I was aiming to show both one person teaching another, and also "
"doing so across national lines without having to travel all the way across "
"the world, since reducing travel to cut down on emissions by using these "
"sorts of \"portals\" is a suggestion I've seen. With one girl in Kenya, the "
"other in Ukraine, they - and other people who come to these spaces, which "
"are meant to be community centers or something akin to that - can connect on "
"a regular basis, form relationships, and teach each other things. In this "
"case it's dance - the Chakacha dance from Mombasa, meant to be danced by "
"women only."
msgstr ""
"For this, I was aiming to show both one person teaching another, and also "
"doing so across national lines without having to travel all the way across "
"the world, since reducing travel to cut down on emissions by using these "
"sorts of \"portals\" is a suggestion I've seen. With one girl in Kenya, the "
"other in Ukraine, they - and other people who come to these spaces, which "
"are meant to be community centers or something akin to that - can connect on "
"a regular basis, form relationships, and teach each other things. In this "
"case it's dance - the Chakacha dance from Mombasa, meant to be danced by "
"women only."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/rehearsal-at-portal/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The wall art on the left is inspired by a mask made by Cyrus Kabiru, a "
"Kenyan artist that crafts intricate masks out of discarded materials, and "
"the hairstyle is similar to one in a Thandiwe Muriu photograph. The wall art "
"on the right side of the screen is based on the paintings of Maria "
"Prymachenko, a renowned Ukrainian artist who lived in the 20th century."
msgstr ""
"The wall art on the left is inspired by a mask made by Cyrus Kabiru, a "
"Kenyan artist that crafts intricate masks out of discarded materials, and "
"the hairstyle is similar to one in a Thandiwe Muriu photograph. The wall art "
"on the right side of the screen is based on the paintings of Maria "
"Prymachenko, a renowned Ukrainian artist who lived in the 20th century."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/tailors/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Tailors"
msgstr "Krawcy"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/tailors/index.en.md
msgid ""
"An illustration to one of the Solarpunk Prompts episodes, [The Tailors]"
"(https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-tailors) "
"[[transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-"
"Tailors)]:"
msgstr ""
"Ilustracja do jednego z odcinków podcastu Solarpunk Prompts, [The Tailors]"
"(https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-tailors) "
"[[transkrypt](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-"
"Tailors)]:"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/tailors/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A new Tailor joins a community which has lacked one for years. In a world of distributed manufacturing tailors are no longer just artisans, but educators, material and sustainability experts, fashion designers and translators of cultures, making sure no garment offends others when traveling. Seeing that they’re much less traditional than their predecessor, will they be accepted by the community? Which bold statement surprised everybody?\n"
msgstr "> Nowy Krawiec dołącza do społeczności która od lat radziła sobie bez nich. W świecie zdystrybuowanej produkcji to już nie tylko rzemieślnicy, ale edukatorzy, eksperci w sprawach materiałów i odżywalności, projektanci mody i tłumacze kultur zapewniający, że strój nikogo nie urazi w trakcie podróży. Czy społeczność przyjmie z otwartymi ramionami nowego Krawca, widząc, że jest on / ona znacznie mniej konserwatywny/a niż jego/jej poprzednik sprzed lat? Jakie śmiałe posunięcie zszokowało wszystkich?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/tailors/index.en.md
msgid "Based on the [story seed](/seeds/the-tailors)."
msgstr "Na bazie [zalążka opowieści](/pl/seeds/the-tailors)."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/tower/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Tower"
msgstr "Drewniany blok mieszkalny"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/tower/index.en.md
msgid ""
"An illustration to one of the Solarpunk Prompts episodes, [The Tower]"
"(https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-tower) "
"[[transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-"
"Tower)]:"
msgstr ""
"Ilustracja do jednego z odcinków podcastu Solarpunk Prompts, [Wieży](https://"
"podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-tower) [[transkrpt]"
"(https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Tower)]:"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/tower/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A community is freshly moved into a new, wooden, sustainable, climate-controlled tower designed to help them be close to each other and live communally. For some it is a dream come true, for others it is a culture shock, but everyone is struggling with the trauma of losing their old homes to floods, fires and relocation programs. While the adults deal with their emotions, children are quick to run around and explore the wonders of their new home.\n"
msgstr "> Społeczność świeżo wprowadziła się do nowego, drewnianego, odżywalnego i udopornionego na zmiany klimatu bloku mieszkalnego. Został on zaprojektowany, by pomóc im stworzyć wspólnotę i zbliżyć się do siebie nawzajem. Dla części mieszkańców jest to szczyt marzeń, podczas gdy inni mierzą się z szokiem kulturowym. Wszyscy z nich stracili swoje poprzednie domy w pożarach, powodziach i programach przesiedleniowych. Kiedy dorośli stawiają czoła trudnym emocjom, ich dzieci z radością eksplorują fascynujące zakamarki budynku.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/tower/index.en.md
msgid "Based on the [story seed](/seeds/the-tower)."
msgstr "Na bazie [zalążka opowieści](/pl/seeds/the-tower)."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/tower/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The illustration itself is a collaboration between The Lemonaut (lineart, "
"characters, colors) and Scandinavian101 (architecture, wooden construction "
"research)."
msgstr ""
"Ilustracja powstała we współpracy pomiędzy The Lemonaut (linia, postaci, "
"kolory) i Scandinavian101 (architektura, źródła o konstrukcjach drewnianych)."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/ukrainian-steppe/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ukrainian Steppe"
msgstr "Ukraiński Step"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/ukrainian-steppe/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Originally a submission to Andrewism's [Solarpunk Art Collab 2023](https://"
"andrew-ism.tumblr.com/post/741342402945646592/solarpunk-art-2023-"
"bioregions), the illustration depicts a temperate grassland in Ukraine."
msgstr ""
"Originally a submission to Andrewism's [Solarpunk Art Collab 2023](https://"
"andrew-ism.tumblr.com/post/741342402945646592/solarpunk-art-2023-"
"bioregions), the illustration depicts a temperate grassland in Ukraine."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/ukrainian-steppe/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The region depicted is the Ukrainian steppe (Temperate Grasslands biome). It's a rapidly disappearing region, as most of the land gets turned into crop fields or forest to provide profit with little regard for the ecosystem. At the top part of the drawing is a bus stop in the rural area near a maize field. Ukraine grows a lot of maize, mostly to provide feed for the meat industry, so rewilding it back into a grassland would be a great way to help achieve degrowth and heal the environment. Also fertilizer use often leads to eutrophication - the green puddle to the left is a small example of that. The country's ecosystems are also being wrecked by the Russian invasion. Helping the land recover from both profit-oriented industry and war is undoubtedly an important step towards Solarpunk.\n"
"> \n"
"> The bus stop is now a pleasant little space to pass the time when getting from one place to the next. It's even got a small solar-powered community fridge and some wall art in the traditional Petrykivka style.\n"
msgstr ""
"> The region depicted is the Ukrainian steppe (Temperate Grasslands biome). It's a rapidly disappearing region, as most of the land gets turned into crop fields or forest to provide profit with little regard for the ecosystem. At the top part of the drawing is a bus stop in the rural area near a maize field. Ukraine grows a lot of maize, mostly to provide feed for the meat industry, so rewilding it back into a grassland would be a great way to help achieve degrowth and heal the environment. Also fertilizer use often leads to eutrophication - the green puddle to the left is a small example of that. The country's ecosystems are also being wrecked by the Russian invasion. Helping the land recover from both profit-oriented industry and war is undoubtedly an important step towards Solarpunk.\n"
"> \n"
"> The bus stop is now a pleasant little space to pass the time when getting from one place to the next. It's even got a small solar-powered community fridge and some wall art in the traditional Petrykivka style.\n"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/youth-dorm/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Youth dorm in New Spark"
msgstr "Akademik w Nowej Iskrze"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/the-lemonaut/youth-dorm/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> A place where young people can go live if they want to have more independence from their elders and try to figure themselves out. It's not a place of complete isolation from society, but a sort of refuge. Nobody is forced to live here, and it's not tied to any one institution like a school or college. Older people are still allowed to enter and hang around, but are asked to respect the social norms outlined by the residents.\n"
"> \n"
"> One apartment can often have at least two people living in it, but some prefer to have their personal space. When a person feels they've outgrown the dorm or that others need it more than them right now, they can move out - and clean the place up for the next resident. There's lots of history in these walls, in every nonsensical graffiti, crooked piece of pottery in the kitchens, and the inside jokes passed down from one generation to the next.\n"
"> \n"
"> The dorm is (meant to be) shaped as a hexagon, forming an open space so light can enter through the middle. There's shared kitchens, a place to do arts and crafts, a gym, a mess hall, a laundromat, a ground-level bathroom (in addition to the ones in the apartments), both an elevator and stairs. The whole place is wheelchair-accessible and each apartment has the necessary accommodations.\n"
"> \n"
"> Before a person goes to live in such a dorm, their community makes sure they know basic safety rules. They likely already know how to cook at least a few types of meals, do laundry and dishes, practice hygiene, understand safe sex practices, know how to clean stuff, do basic first aid, things like that. At least once a year, drills are organized to make sure everyone knows what to do and how to help each other in an emergency. The rest is left up to them to decide.\n"
msgstr ""
"> A place where young people can go live if they want to have more independence from their elders and try to figure themselves out. It's not a place of complete isolation from society, but a sort of refuge. Nobody is forced to live here, and it's not tied to any one institution like a school or college. Older people are still allowed to enter and hang around, but are asked to respect the social norms outlined by the residents.\n"
"> \n"
"> One apartment can often have at least two people living in it, but some prefer to have their personal space. When a person feels they've outgrown the dorm or that others need it more than them right now, they can move out - and clean the place up for the next resident. There's lots of history in these walls, in every nonsensical graffiti, crooked piece of pottery in the kitchens, and the inside jokes passed down from one generation to the next.\n"
"> \n"
"> The dorm is (meant to be) shaped as a hexagon, forming an open space so light can enter through the middle. There's shared kitchens, a place to do arts and crafts, a gym, a mess hall, a laundromat, a ground-level bathroom (in addition to the ones in the apartments), both an elevator and stairs. The whole place is wheelchair-accessible and each apartment has the necessary accommodations.\n"
"> \n"
"> Before a person goes to live in such a dorm, their community makes sure they know basic safety rules. They likely already know how to cook at least a few types of meals, do laundry and dishes, practice hygiene, understand safe sex practices, know how to clean stuff, do basic first aid, things like that. At least once a year, drills are organized to make sure everyone knows what to do and how to help each other in an emergency. The rest is left up to them to decide.\n"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/vizuza/dozynki-harvest-festival-in-kashubia/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dożynki - Harvest Festival in Kashubia, Poland"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/vizuza/dozynki-harvest-festival-in-kashubia/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The annual Harvest Festival descends from the centuries-old Polish and "
"Kashubian harvest celebrations, held by the end of summer. It is no longer "
"only a celebration of crops, but a place to strengthen resilience and "
"promote mutual aid. The traditional time of Harvest Festival, the end of "
"summer, is also the driest time of the year, with the biggest wildfire "
"impact, so there is a seed exchange event with many of the seeds being saved "
"and used to regenerate the burnt areas."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/vizuza/dozynki-harvest-festival-in-kashubia/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Farms operate through community-supported partnerships. Residents purchase "
"shares in local farms - sharing both the harvests and the risks of a "
"difficult growing season. If drought or fire destroys crops, members can "
"choose to accept community credits instead of produce, helping farmers to "
"recover. In the illustration, we can see the farmer's booths/stands and "
"people gathered around them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/vizuza/dozynki-harvest-festival-in-kashubia/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Wildfire prevention has become a major community effort. Instead of relying "
"solely on cleared firebreaks (\"fuel breaks\"), residents have created "
"living resilience corridors (\"fuel break matrix\") throughout the "
"landscape. Wetlands, ponds, community gardens, orchards, and hugelkultur "
"mounds built from decaying wood help retain water, support biodiversity, and "
"slow the spread of fire. It's visible in the surrounding landscape."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/vizuza/dozynki-harvest-festival-in-kashubia/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The scars of a recent wildfire are still visible during this year's "
"festival. Burned tree trunks stand on the horizon. Partially charred logs "
"are being repurposed into new hugelkultur beds (hugelkultur - a raised "
"garden mound built from buried logs, branches, and organic matter that "
"stores water and slowly releases nutrients as it decomposes)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/vizuza/dozynki-harvest-festival-in-kashubia/index.en.md
msgid ""
"One of the most recognizable groups present in the festival is the Beaver "
"People Guild. Decades earlier, they began as volunteers working to reverse "
"generations of drainage and forest melioration. By filling abandoned "
"drainage ditches, restoring wetlands, and increasing the land's ability to "
"retain water, they helped bring moisture back into the landscape. What began "
"as a grassroots movement has since become a respected civic institution. The "
"beaver has become a symbol of ecological restoration throughout the region."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/vizuza/dozynki-harvest-festival-in-kashubia/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Last but not least, there is music present all throughout the festival, "
"which helps people connect and relieve their hardships.  Many activities and "
"actions during the festival radiate around water, because this element is "
"the \"protagonist\" of this world."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/xulia-vicente/earth-water-air/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Earth, water, air"
msgstr "Ziemia, woda, powietrze"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/xulia-vicente/earth-water-air/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk scene on a sunny wheat field, where some small robots do the "
"harvest while a kid is reading on a woman's lap. The community works on "
"building wind energy while also having some free time to enjoy themselves. "
"All three elements of the title are reunited and sourced sustainably in the "
"image."
msgstr ""
"Solarpunkowa scena na słonecznym polu pszenicy, gdzie małe roboty pracują "
"nad żniewami a na kolanach kobiety małe dziecko czyta książkę. Społeczność "
"pracuje nad zbudowaniem energii wiatrowej dając sobie jednocześnie czas na "
"zabawę. Wszystkie trzy żywioły tytułu łączą się w odżywalną całość na "
"ilustracji."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/xulia-vicente/earth-water-air/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The [illustration](https://xuliavicente.com/project/utopies/) was created "
"for the exhibition Utopies, curated by [APIV – The Illustrators’ Association "
"of Valencia](https://apiv.com/)."
msgstr ""
"[Ilustracja](https://xuliavicente.com/project/utopies/) została stworzona na "
"wystawę \"Utopie\" kurowaną przez [APIV – The Illustrators’ Association of "
"Valencia](https://apiv.com/)."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/art/yuuna-maiko/harvest-of-knowledge/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Harvest of Knowledge"
msgstr "Żniwa Wiedzy"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/yuuna-maiko/harvest-of-knowledge/index.en.md
msgid ""
"In the heart of a lush orchard, a grandfather shares his knowledge with his "
"granddaughter, showing her how an apple-harvesting robot works.  Perched on "
"the back of a gentle yak, the child listens with wonder, her eyes sparkling "
"with curiosity."
msgstr ""
"W sercu zielonego bujnego sadu dziadek dzieli się swoją wiedzą ze swoją "
"wnuczką pokazując jej, jak działa robot zbierający jabłka. Siedząc na "
"łagodnym jaku dziecko słucha zadziwione, a jej oczy błyszczą ciekawością."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/art/yuuna-maiko/harvest-of-knowledge/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This sunlit scene highlights a gentle transmission of knowledge between "
"generations, where nature, technology, and humanity coexist in harmony."
msgstr ""
"Ta słoneczna scena ukazuje subtelność przekazywania wiedzy między "
"pokoleniami, gdzie natura, technologia i ludzkość współistnieją w harmonii."
